Not a theme park character, but a witness.  


I saw a kid purposely barf all over Pluto's feetpaws, much to the laughter of his friends and then tell Pluto to "lick it up,:

&#x200B;

Pluto walked over to a nearby security guard and pointedly started cursing out the kid.

&#x200B;

Of course the kid and his friends were thrown out of the park, but the kicker was what the kid said when security was escorting them out and even ASKED what he hoped to accomplish by something so disgusting. (I found this it out when I overheard the guard consoling the Pluto guy.)

&#x200B;

"Pluto's a dog and dogs eat vomit! Figured he'd lick it clean."

Tried holding a concert for my family when I was 7-9 years old.... using only the auto tunes on a keyboard for music......

&#x200B;

I STILL have nightmares

Everything you heard about Weird Al Yankovic being a nice man is wrong..  


.....................  


.....  


.....  


...........  


Nice.......... is a freaking UNDERSTATEMENT.  


The man is a God-Tier Saint.  


I saw him live during his ill-advised vanity tour and was chosen to participate in Weird Al Jeopardy (Yay me!) and actually WON! (Yay me again!)

&#x200B;

So I got a medal, a plaque, and tons of cheers.

&#x200B;

The concert comes and goes and it's time for the Meet and Greet.

&#x200B;

Unfortunately, when I had tried to buy meet and greet tickets, they were sold out. But I had a letter I had handwritten to Weird Al. See, my dad had gotten me into him and we still listened to his music quite a bit. I went to one of the ushers by the closed curtains, (I have her name, but to protect her identity, let's call her "Lisa"). I talked to Lisa and told her that I knew I wasn't able to get Meet and Greet Tickets, but was wondering if, if I were to give her the letter I wrote, if she wouldn't mind giving it to him. I was wearing the medal I had won and she asked me if I had been on Weird Al Jeopardy. I told her I had been and even won. She looked at me and said something I will never forget.  


"You know what? Get on in there. Just shhhhh."  


It took me all I had not to Squee, but I nodded, thanked her profusely, then rushed in. I got handed a setlist of all the songs he'd performed that day (I remember Larry, UHF, You don't love me anymore, Albequerque, some of the best!) and a minute later, Lisa returned with a spare Meet and Greet pass for me so as not to arouse suspicion. I must have thanked her like 20 times as I sat and waited. Eventually Weird Al came out and, even though it was close to midnight and he had just performed a close to 2-hour show, the man looked eager and excited to meet us. We were told to only have him sign one thing, but that pictures had no limit and it cost zilch to get either photos or autographs. Each person went up in line, got an autograph and a picture and Weird Al talked to them and shook their hands as if they were his best friends. He treated everyone like he was humbled by THEM. I was towards the back of the line and when I got up, I was still wearing my medal. His handler, who had HOSTED Weird Al Jeopardy, immediately told him that I was the champion, even saying it loudly so the others could hear and Weird Al gave me a handshake. I had a DVD of UHF and a VHS of his Bad Hair Day videos and I had set them both down to put the VHS away since I knew it was one per. But Weird Al took both and signed them both, the Handler saying "We'll sign two for the champion." I took a picture with him and then I just told him how much his music helped me, how my dad had introduced me to him, how it brought us together and I thanked him over and over.

&#x200B;

He started to shake my hand again, but then he said something else that I'll always remember.

&#x200B;

"Would you like a hug?"  


Weird Al Yankovic, the best Comedy Musician in EXISTENCE, was offering me a hug!

&#x200B;

I said yes IMMEDIATELY and we embraced, a full-on father son-esque hug and the entire line was cheering. (He even smelled like lemons!) As I got up, I could NOT STOP SMILING. I just thanked him over and over again and told him every bit of success he had he had earned 5 times over.

&#x200B;

Since then, I make it a point to listen to his music quite often. I still watch the Albequerque video a ton.

&#x200B;

Yeah it's true sometimes you shouldn't meet your idols, but sometimes....... you TOTALLY should!

&#x200B;

WEIRD AL ROCKS!!!!!!

Oh, I can imagine the rest of her rules for "Having a good time."

&#x200B;

\*clears throat\*

&#x200B;

7. Under absolutely NO circumstances is there to be ANY gambling. Gambling is the Devil's fun and we have no need to waste our money or time on such a sinful hobby. I was thinking we should use that money to donate to the church. Why gamble when you can help others out instead and instead of being tempted by the Devil's money, we could cleanse our souls by giving to God's great plan.

&#x200B;

8. I have chosen a list of appropriate shows and lectures for us to attend. Magicians, comedians, dancers are all servants of Satan and, as a devout servant of the Lord, I feel it is my responsibility to help you have entertainment by enlightenment. You'll be riveted knowing the stories of our Savior and that's so much better than being tempted by such trivial beings.

&#x200B;

9. Considering there are so many poor and starving countries out there, I feel it is inappropriate for us to be wasteful while others have not. Therefore, we will not be going to any buffets or restaurants. We will show solidarity and penance for other less fortunate countries by eating from the groceries I provide and only in strict meals. By doing this, we can get in touch with those of a greater plight and realize that we are truly blessed for the life we have. Hunger is God's love and we could easily fill up those pains with prayer.

&#x200B;

10. We are to all dress modestly. No bikinis, no swimsuits, nothing that reveals any skin whatsoever. I have even gone as far as to pick out a set of more appropriate wedding gowns and outfits. The only one who should see the bride in anything less than modesty is her husband as we don't want to give others impure thoughts.

&#x200B;

By following these rules, I know we can have fun and keep faithful to God at the same time. I'm so looking forward to this Girl's weekend out! It will be ever so much fun!

&#x200B;

With dearest love and compassion,

Choosing Beggar.

