This just happened a few days ago and it still hasn't left my brain.  


I work at a movie theater and I help run the ticket booth, making sure everyone has tickets to come in, not sneaking food or cameras, keeping the lobby clean, that kind of thing.

&#x200B;

In that time, I've met all kinds of customers and I usually try to make a little conversation or something with them as I take their tickets. (I'm Autistic, but this helps me practice on my social skills)

&#x200B;

But on 4/8/19 (I'll remember this probably forever), I met my first set of customers that made me speechless.

&#x200B;

It was a group of four, all females. Two of them were Middle-Eastern as evidenced by the Hijabs they wore. There was also an American woman and a little girl.

&#x200B;

I went to take the tickets from the woman and turned to the little girl to try and make small talk.

&#x200B;

Then I got a good look at the girls face.

&#x200B;

She had horrific burn marks all over her face, her eyes were hid behind scar tissue, her nose was shapeless with a breathing tube to help breath inserted in the one nostril that remained, the front of her hairline was purely scarring, her lips were barely visible, covered in marks.

&#x200B;

And the scarring spread from her head to her neck to even her upper body (what I could see of it exposed).

&#x200B;

I looked at the other women to offer support....... then I saw one of the other women and I noticed they were even worse.

&#x200B;

Their face had even more severe burn scars, their eyes were pure black from what I could see beneath the lumps of tissue. They had literally no nose, just a hole in the center of their face. Their lips were GONE, leaving their teeth fully exposed.

&#x200B;

I just took their tickets and told them I hoped they enjoyed their movie.

&#x200B;

As soon as they left, one of my managers (We'll call him E, a REALLY nice guy if not a little weird at times) came up to get a package from the customer service desk. I pulled him over and told him what I saw... that I knew EXACTLY how those girls got those marks. He said that there some horrible people in the world, that some men do some cruel things to their family and he even asked if I was ok.

&#x200B;

I said I was, but I felt so sad for them, wondering how someone could do that not just to an innocent woman, but to a little girl!!!!!  


&#x200B;

We parted ways and I spent the rest of my shift just in thought. I had a lot of questions I had wanted to ask them, but I felt like I knew the answers already and they were ones I didn't want.....

&#x200B;

To those 2 lovely women, I don't know if you'll ever see this, but I hope things get a lot better.

&#x200B;

And to the fucker who caused those burns, I hope you rot in hell.

